[medium] collector.go:628 (correctness)
attachSecretsManagerEvents indexes identifiers as map[string]string, so when IncludePlannedDeletion returns an active secret and a pending-deletion/recreated secret with the same friendly name, the shared friendly-name identifier overwrites one ARN nondeterministically. A CloudTrail event whose raw JSON contains only the friendly name then attaches to just one arbitrary record, which can put recovery_window_days or rotation/update evidence on the wrong secret and omit it from the other.
Suggested fix: Change the identifier index to preserve all matching ARNs, for example map[string][]string, and attach an event to every ARN matched by a non-unique friendly-name identifier while still de-duplicating by event_id+ARN. Prefer exact ARN/full resource_id matches when present, but do not collapse shared friendly-name matches to one ARN.
Guidance: In collector.go, rewrite attachSecretsManagerEvents so the identifier index does not collapse multiple ARNs onto one string key. Replace the current map[string]string identifiers with a structure that keeps all candidates per identifier, e.g. map[string]map[string]bool or map[string][]string plus an addIdentifier helper. Add ARN and full secretIDFromARN identifiers as high-confidence identifiers, and add secretNameWithoutSuffix(id) / d.name as potentially non-unique identifiers without overwriting earlier ARNs. When scanning each event.raw, attach the normalized event to every ARN matched by every contained identifier, using the existing event_id + "\x00" + arn de-dup key so the same event is not appended twice to the same secret. Preserve the deliberate raw JSON substring matching and the DeleteSecret recovery_window_days enrichment, but make that enrichment happen per matched ARN. Add a collector test with two drafts/secrets sharing the same friendly name but different ARN suffixes and a CloudTrail event containing only the friendly name; assert both records receive the event and neither record is dropped due to map overwrite. Do not strip or change resource_id; the full ARN suffix remains intentional.
